Intercepting routes start with `(`: `(.)` means same level, `(..)` one level up, `(..)(..)` two levels up, `(...)` from root.

In the classic pattern, `app/feed/@modal/(.)photo/[id]/page.tsx` intercepts `app/photo/[id]/page.tsx` when navigation originates from `/feed`.


| Convention | Matches | Typical use |
|---|---|---|
| `(.)segment` | same level | feed → photo modal |
| `(..)segment` | one level up | `/dashboard/photo` from anywhere |
| `(...)segment` | from root | global modal |
| Pairing | needs `@slot` | layout receives `modal` prop |
| Refresh | bypasses intercept | renders real `photo/[id]` page |

**Interview Tip:** Recite the 4 levels `(.), (..),  (..)(..), (...)` and stress client-nav-only: refresh shows the real page. That nuance wins points.

