`instrumentation.ts` (or `.js`) at the project root exports `export async function register() { ...

}`. Next calls it once when the Node server (and separately the Edge runtime if you have `edge` routes/middleware) boots — before any request.


| Hook | When | Runtime | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `instrumentation.ts register()` | server boot once | Node + Edge | init OTEL/Sentry |
| `onRequestError` | per error | Node/Edge | capture route error + request |
| `instrumentation-client.ts` | browser navigation | client | RUM, router events |
| `instrumentationHook` | config flag | both | enable hook (default true in 15) |

**Interview Tip:** Distinguish boot vs per-request: `register` is boot-only (no cookies), `onRequestError` is per-request with context. OTEL/`@vercel/otel` is the buzzword.

```js
// instrumentation.ts — Next 15
import * as Sentry from '@sentry/nextjs';
export async function register(){
  if (process.env.NEXT_RUNTIME === 'nodejs') {
    await import('./sentry.server.config');
    const { registerOTel } = await import('@vercel/otel');
    registerOTel({ serviceName: 'web' });
  }
}
export function onRequestError(err: unknown, request: Request, ctx: { routerKind: string; routePath: string }){
  Sentry.captureRequestError(err, { path: ctx.routePath });
  console.error(`[${ctx.routePath}]`, err);
}
```

