Next 15 has built-in OpenTelemetry instrumentation: `npm i @vercel/otel @opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http`, then in `instrumentation.ts` `export function register() { registerOTel({ serviceName: 'web', spanProcessors: [...] }) }`.

With `experimental.


| Step | File | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| Install | `package.json` | `@vercel/otel`, OTEL exporter |
| Register | `instrumentation.ts` | `registerOTel({ serviceName })` once |
| Auto | — | spans for RSC, fetch, middleware |
| Custom | any Server Component | `trace.getTracer().startActiveSpan` |
| Export | env var | `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` |

**Interview Tip:** Name the flow: `registerOTel` in `register()` + auto RSC/fetch spans + custom `tracer.startActiveSpan` — shows production OTEL, not just console.log.

```js
// instrumentation.ts — OTEL with Vercel helper
import { registerOTel } from '@vercel/otel';
export function register(){
  registerOTel({ serviceName: 'web-shop' });
}
// app/lib/db.ts — custom span
import { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api';
const tracer = trace.getTracer('db');
export async function getUser(id:string){
  return tracer.startActiveSpan('db.getUser', async (span)=>{
    span.setAttribute('user.id', id);
    const u = await prisma.user.findUnique({ where:{id}});
    span.end(); return u;
  });
}
```
